    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d585-a1">

                <pb facs="1001" n="905" xml:id="pg905"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Rumanian Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Duca</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-02-15"><hi rendition="#italic">February 15,
                        1926</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: Referring to this Legation’s Note
                    No. 152 of January 6th last,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d585-f1"/> addressed to Your
                    Excellency relative to the bill-of-law regarding the so-called “embatic” lands,
                    I have the honor to inform Your Excellency that I am now instructed to
                    supplement the representations made in that Note by the statement that my
                    Government would view with concern any action on the part of the Rumanian
                    authorities that would prejudice American interests in subsoil rights acquired
                    in good faith and in accordance with the law of Rumania.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. S. Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
